===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|id=cut|*-mos|*-mós}}
From {{suffix|en|crony|t1=close friend|ism|pos2={{glossary|suffix}} forming names of a tendency of action, behaviour, condition, opinion, or state belonging to a class or group of persons}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=7168471402|date=July 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220824040140/https://www.lexico.com/definition/cronyism}}</ref>

