===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|originally|US|derogatory}} [[favouritism|Favouritism]] to [[friend#Noun|friends]] without [[regard#Noun|regard]] for their [[qualification]]s; especially {{lb|en|politics}}, in their [[appointment]] to [[political#Adjective|political]] [[position#Noun|positions]].
#: {{coordinate terms|en|nepotism|patronage}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Randall G. Holcombe; Andrea M. Castillo|title=Liberalism and Cronyism: Two Rival Political and Economic Systems|publisher=Mercatus Center at George Mason University|year=2013|isbn=9780989219303|passage=Because of this centralized command structure, communist societies fall prey to the forces of '''cronyism''' and influence-peddling as commune members without economic power curry favor with commune leaders that control access to resources.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Thomas J. Gradel; Dick Simpson|title=Corrupt Illinois: Patronage, Cronyism, and Criminality|publisher=University of Illinois Press|year=2015|page=117|isbn=9780252097034|passage=Patronage, nepotism, '''cronyism''', abuse of power, and criminal activity flourish,  sometimes for decades, in numerous town halls, police stations, and special-purpose government agencies in the suburbs.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} The [[condition#Noun|condition]] of being friends; [[friendship]]; also, the [[ability]] or [[inclination]] to [[make#Verb|make]] friends.

